# Security headers for the app site (app.retain-growth.ai).
# Copied into web/dist/_headers by the build command in netlify.toml, so they
# ship with every production deploy — and only there: `netlify dev` reads
# _headers from its own [dev] publish dir (web/public), where this file
# isn't, so local Vite (inline Fast Refresh preamble, HMR websocket) runs
# without a CSP.
#
# Netlify merges every rule matching a path, and two Content-Security-Policy
# headers are BOTH enforced (the stricter wins) — so the CSP is never in the
# catch-all /* rule: app routes get the strict one, /lp/* its own looser one
# that allows the Meta/TikTok/Google pixels (see git history of netlify.toml
# for the reasoning behind each source).

# Permissions-Policy microphone=(self): voice notes recorded in the funnel builder.
/*
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), geolocation=(), payment=(), usb=(), microphone=(self)

